      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the absence of arm weakness or pain is reassuring, facial drooping alone is a critical sign of a stroke that can have no warning symptoms before sudden onset. Bell's palsy is also possible, but only a doctor can distinguish between the two safely and quickly. Definitely do not just take vitamins and wait it out; please call ahead to your local emergency number or drive to the ER immediately to get a proper stroke evaluation. Given the risks, getting checked right away is the safest choice to protect your eye and nerve function.",
